  "method": "Fixed independent 16384 full-game trials per candidate and policy, 512 paired blocks of 32, 163840 games total. Both retained 41$-44 candidates under five policies. Shared dice across candidates and policies; every seed disjoint from preceding studies and timing/validation samples. Cube strength stays at GNUbg 2-ply; checker policies vary normal 2-ply, huge-filter 2-ply, large-filter 3-ply throughout every full game. Identical 1-ply control-variate evaluations across all policies; no dice rotation, fixed-turn cutoff, late policy reduction, pooling, optional stopping, or reference-value correction. Exact two-sided bearoff evaluation remains eligible. XG rules mean money/Jacoby/beaver/raccoon, original responder retains ownership, cube ceiling 1024. Actual legal cube branches are separately evaluated; future search-node beaver backups use scale-invariant continuation approximations. Five paired move gaps and four differences of gaps have separate simultaneous 95% Student-t families. Eight per-candidate policy effects form a third family. Absolute differences against published XG EVs are descriptive; original XG margins retained. Selection follows the previous completed experiment; this is one diagnostic position, not an all-openings accuracy claim."
